      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The quoting process and installation was fine and all the above issues were met in a timely and pleasant manner.However the after sales service has been almost non existent.  My first phone call was promptly returned.On October 27 our inverter disconnected from Wi-fi.  Of course we did not understand why and the repercussions thereof, so I phoned SGS at 7.52am and left a message.  With no response to my call I phoned again at 11.01 to the mobile and at 11.38 to landline no.  I was understandably anxious.  My calls were returned at 12.06 pm and clearly not well received.  I was told that \"I told you I would always get back to you.  If you expect me to keep coming out to you there will have to be charges involved.  I took this as a veiled threat and am reluctant to call again.  I had not asked or expected him to come out to me; I was just after some explanation.  He sent me a link to reconnect, but despite many many attempts this did not happen.  I let him know this and he said he would send someone around that day.  He later sent a text to say they had had a big day and would not be coming. The next day the inverter was up and running again and was described as a \"glitch\".  On November, I advised that the inverter again disconnected from the Wi-f and that once again that I had followed the instructions to reconnect  but again could not effect reconnection.  He contacted me on Monday and said someone would come around that morning and I told him I was not home till after 1.00pm.  Still have not had any follow up.I decided to put in an enquiry direct to Goodwe.  And when doing this on or about 18 or 19/11 I went out to check the Serial no and discovered that the inverter was again disconnected from Wi-fi.  3 times in this short period of time signals more that a \"glitch\".  Particularly as everything else was still connected.If I don't get a favorable response from Goodwe, my next step will have to be Fair Trading/Obudsman.  I have paid out good money and don't think my expectations are too high.To add insult to injury before the installation I enquired about a Sungro inverter but was told they were not available in 3 phase which I later found out was incorrect.  No happy Jan.",
